  "readout": {
    "readout_answer": "36",
    "readout_text": "To solve the given system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\ny^3 = x^2 \\\\\n(y - x)^2 = 4y^2\n\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nwe aim to find the value of $ x + y $, where $ x $ and $ y $ are positive real numbers.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Express $ x $ in terms of $ y $\n\nFrom the first equation:\n\n$$\ny^3 = x^2 \\Rightarrow x = y^{3/2}\n$$\n\nWe use this expression for $ x $ in the second equation.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Substitute into the second equation\n\n$$\n(y - x)^2 = 4y^2\n$$\n\nSubstitute $ x = y^{3/2} $:\n\n$$\n(y - y^{3/2})^2 = 4y^2\n$$\n\nNow expand the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n(y - y^{3/2})^2 = y^2 - 2y \\cdot y^{3/2} + (y^{3/2})^2 = y^2 - 2y^{5/2} + y^3\n$$\n\nSo the equation becomes:\n\n$$\ny^2 - 2y^{5/2} + y^3 = 4y^2\n$$\n\nBring all terms to one side:\n\n$$\ny^3 + y^2 - 2y^{5/2} - 4y^2 = 0\n\\Rightarrow y^3 - 3y^2 - 2y^{5/2} = 0\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Factor the equation\n\nFactor out $ y^2 $:\n\n$$\ny^2(y - 3 - 2y^{1/2}) = 0\n$$\n\nSince $ y > 0 $, $ y^2 \\neq 0 $, so we solve:\n\n$$\ny - 3 - 2\\sqrt{y} = 0\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Solve the simplified equation\n\nLet $ t = \\sqrt{y} $, so $ y = t^2 $. Substitute into the equation:\n\n$$\nt^2 - 2t - 3 = 0\n$$\n\nSolve the quadratic:\n\n$$\nt = \\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^2 - 4(1)(-3)}}{2(1)} = \\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{4 + 12}}{2} = \\frac{2 \\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} = \\frac{2 \\pm 4}{2}\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\nt = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad t = -1\n$$\n\nSince $ t = \\sqrt{y} > 0 $, we take $ t = 3 $, so:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{y} = 3 \\Rightarrow y = 9\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Find $ x $ and compute $ x + y $\n\nFrom the first equation:\n\n$$\nx^2 = y^3 = 9^3 = 729 \\Rightarrow x = \\sqrt{729} = 27\n$$\n\nThus:\n\n$$\nx + y = 27 + 9 = \\boxed{36}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{36}\n$$",
